#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Integrates AMENDMENT_A6..A10 into SECTION5_PROTOCOL.md and marks it FROZEN. The original draft is first preserved byte-identical as SECTION5_PROTOCOL_v0_DRAFT.md (hash 8abd...).
Consolidation only: no rule is added; where an amendment is silent the draft text applies; where they conflict the later amendment prevails. Writes the sidecar. Refuses to run twice."""
import hashlib, datetime, shutil
from pathlib import Path
from zoneinfo import ZoneInfo

ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent; P = ROOT / "SECTION5_PROTOCOL.md"; V0 = ROOT / "SECTION5_PROTOCOL_v0_DRAFT.md"
sha = lambda p: hashlib.sha256(Path(p).read_bytes()).hexdigest(); OLD = "8abd20f3557dac0991e30ea8c2807aee35be9d7de1c79b199d7f371397c97479"
assert sha(V0) == OLD, "v0 copy must equal the original draft"; assert sha(P) == OLD, "protocol already integrated"
orig = P.read_text(encoding="utf-8"); inputs = orig[orig.index("## Cited inputs"):orig.index("## Protocol text (verbatim)")].rstrip()
now = datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc)
am = [("A6", "AMENDMENT_A6.md", "event rule, H1(a) metric, Section 6 thresholds, BOCPD secondary, grids and baseline, stable days, pool 80"), ("A7", "AMENDMENT_A7.md", "continuous thresholds and bisection"),
      ("A8", "AMENDMENT_A8.md", "splice scale fix, R=1 gate, contamination and fold exclusion, few-stable-days skip, N.3 justification, H1(c)"), ("A8.1", "AMENDMENT_A8_1.md", "gate reference = R=1 placebo"),
      ("A8.2", "AMENDMENT_A8_2.md", "gate bootstrap over stable days; D6 descriptive"), ("A8.3", "AMENDMENT_A8_3.md", "gate characterization, 20 seeds"), ("A8.4", "AMENDMENT_A8_4.md", "multiplicity and leave-one-day-out"),
      ("A9", "AMENDMENT_A9.md", "Holm over 3 families, H2 simplicity order, p-value and rounding confirmed"), ("A10", "AMENDMENT_A10.md", "data backend; machinery check on contaminated folds")]
T = f"""# Section 5 protocol

**Status: FROZEN** (integrated through Amendment A10).

Frozen {now.isoformat()} UTC ({now.astimezone(ZoneInfo('America/New_York')).isoformat()} New York). This file consolidates the original draft and Amendments A6 to A10. It is a consolidation only: no rule was added or changed in the integration. Where an amendment is silent the draft text applies; where they differ the later amendment prevails. The original draft is preserved unchanged as `SECTION5_PROTOCOL_v0_DRAFT.md` (sha256 `{OLD}`; the hash the amendments and reports cite as `SECTION5_PROTOCOL.md`).
Changes from now on: dated, hashed amendments only (A11 onward), each with a ledger row (`METHODS_LEDGER.md`, Section 5 part).

{inputs}

## Amendments integrated (sha256 of each file at integration)

| Amendment | File | Subject | SHA-256 |
|---|---|---|---|
""" + "\n".join(f"| {a} | `{f}` | {s} | `{sha(ROOT / f)}` |" for a, f, s in am) + """

Supporting records (not part of the rules): cold audit `section5_cold_audit.md`, diagnostics D2-D6, pilot reports, gate reports `A8_GATE_REPORT.md`, `A8_1_GATE_REPORT.md`, `A8_2_GATE_REPORT.md`, `A8_3_GATE_CHARACTERIZATION.md`, `A8_4_INVESTIGATION.md`, `A10_MACHINERY_REPORT.md`, all listed with hashes in the Section 5 part of `METHODS_LEDGER.md`.

## Protocol text (effective)

5.0 Scope: detection quality and cross-asset association only; no trading claims. H1 (primary): feature detectors beat returns-only baselines per family on BOTH (a) hit rate versus alarm rate on stable-day splices, metric = partial area under the curve of hit rate against null alarm rate for alarm rates 0-0.5, divided by 0.5 (A6 item 2; replaces the median-delay formulation), and (b) out-of-sample QLIKE for next-60-min SPY volatility; intersection-union test per family, Holm across the THREE H1 families Gaussian HMM, Student-t HMM, HSMM (A6 item 4, A9 item 1). BOCPD is secondary: scored and reported, outside H1 and its Holm family. H1(c), secondary (A8 item 5): detection within 60 min of FOMC 14:00 announcements in uncontaminated test segments, at the frozen alarm frequency, features versus baseline; paired exact sign test, Wilson intervals, outside Holm. H2 (primary): around confirmed calm-to-stressed SPY breaks, TLT/HYG/gold/USD cumulative return from T to T+30 lies outside a placebo distribution matched on time-of-day slot, era and SPY volatility decile (10,000 draws); horizons -30 and +5/15/30/60 min; stressed-to-calm is secondary. S1: return between T_d and T_c versus equal-length placebo. S2: H2 verdict agreement and response correlation across detectors. E1: footprint taxonomy (cite Cieslak & Pang). E2: overnight gaps versus early-session breaks. D1: feature-family selection frequency, including same-family co-selection. Multiple testing: Holm primary, BH secondary, exploratory uncorrected. Features: 4.3.9 matrix v2 by name and hash. Changes: dated, hashed amendments only.

5.1 Folds: 30 LEGACY and 4 RAW TRAIN-only folds (A4); inner train / validation / test with 5-session embargoes (validation and test each lose their first 5 sessions). Inner train fits all parameters, scaling, winsorization 0.5/99.5, Amihud normalization, Lee-Mykland Student-t threshold. Seasonal and relative-volume baselines are already causal. Intraday horizons only.

5.2 Pools: primary 19 (both eras); sensitivity 80 (RAW only; matrix v2 keeps 83 columns, 5.2 drops the three jump_variation__sadj columns, 83 - 3 = 80; A6 item 6c). Enforced exclusions: overnight, raw_volume, log_raw_volume, raw_volume__sadj, response assets, cross-era rows; jump_variation__sadj dropped; Lee-Mykland flag sensitivity-only. Log only if strictly positive in inner train. Every feature model = deseasonalized 5-min return + 1 to 6 selected features; baselines = the deseasonalized 5-min return only, same architecture and hyperparameter budget.

5.3 Decision bars every 5 min (stamped minute 4, 9, ... after 09:30); alarm time = t+1 min. The 5-minute grid is primary; the 1-minute grid (390 updates) and the 15-minute grid are sensitivity analyses on the final setups only. Baseline return input = the 5-minute return divided by the median |5-minute return| of the same grid slot over the previous 20 sessions (>= 10 finite; NaN = skipped update; past sessions only); every model uses this deseasonalized return (A6 item 5). Start at the first grid bar with all features present; abstain before. Session reset (HMM initial probabilities; HSMM state plus duration=1; BOCPD run length 0). No alarms on the first 2 updates. Any missing feature means a skipped update: HMM transition-only; HSMM duration advances with hazard; BOCPD hazard-only, statistics unchanged; no alarms on skips. Last decision: last grid bar with availability at or before the close. Report abstention and skip shares.

5.4 Gaussian HMM diagonal, K 2-4, EM 3 starts, 200 iterations, tol 1e-4, variance floor 1e-6. Student-t HMM via EM with hidden scales, df in [2.1, 30], restart if a state is under 1% occupancy. HSMM K 2-3, free-form durations by EM, durations in elapsed grid intervals capped at the session's scheduled updates, cut off at session end. BOCPD Normal-Gamma per feature (mu0 0, kappa0 1, alpha0 1, beta0 1 on standardized inputs), lambda 12/39/78, run length truncated at 200. Seeds and versions recorded.

5.5 Events. HMM and HSMM (A6 item 1, A7 item 1): old state = argmax at updates 1-2 and at each alarm; alarm (= confirmed event, T_c) when log(s) - log(P(old state)) > theta for 3 consecutive real updates, s = the probability mass outside the old state summed from the other states, theta real on the log-odds scale (thr = 1/(1 + exp(-theta))); T_d = the first of the three; a skipped update resets the count to 0; the first 2 updates are silent; 30-min refractory after an alarm. BOCPD: alarm when the most likely run length falls by at least m updates (m real, >= 1) and then holds 3 updates (`detect_bocpd_map`). Unconfirmed by the close: dropped and counted. States ordered by return variance within each fit. All timestamps at availability time. Direction rule at T_c: SPY 1-min realized variance over [T_d, T_c] versus the 60 min before T_d; above 1 = calm-to-stressed.

5.6 Synthetic splices and thresholds. Splices per fold from the fold's TEST sessions for H1(a) (A6 item 2): stable days only; variance ratios 1.5, 2, 3, 5, 10 (variance ratios), both directions, permanent and 30/60/120-min sandwiches, 24 splices per cell, 400 null splices of two distinct stable days of the same volatility tercile, tau on the 11:05-14:30 grid (<= 14:00 for sandwiches); session A's history for baselines, features recomputed, prices rescaled for continuity. Splice scale (A8 item 1): the post-tau variance of B is expressed in session A's baseline units, so the labelled ratio equals the ratio the detector sees; one factor f per splice applied to every price field of B after tau, volume unchanged. Stable day (A6 item 6b): 390 bars with >= 98% finite closes; deseasonalized 1-min variance = r^2 / median r^2 of the same slot over the previous 20 sessions (>= 10 finite); mean over the last 195 bars / first 195 bars in [0.8, 1.25]; no hourly block mean above 2 times the median block mean. A fold with fewer than 8 stable test days skips H1(a), recorded, without error (A6 item 2, A8 item 3). Curve: for every threshold of the sweep, x = confirmed alarms per null session, y = share of break splices with a confirmed alarm within 60 min after tau; y(x) = the highest y reached at alarm rate <= x; metric = partial area for x in [0, 0.5] divided by 0.5; power by variance ratio reported as the partial area and the hit rate at x = 0.1. The sweep is uniform over theta in [0, 30] step 0.25 and m in [1, 80] step 1 (A7 item 3). This is a sensitivity measure under simulated conditions on real stable days, not real-world detection accuracy. Section 6 event thresholds (A6 item 3, A7 item 2): calibrated on the REAL validation sessions of each fold by bisection so that the detector gives 0.2 confirmed alarms per session (strict end returned; bounds theta [0, 30], m [1, 80]; flags when the strictest bound is above target or the loosest is below it); the realized test-session frequency is reported. BOCPD threshold rule for non-monotone alarms (A6 item 6a): among sweep values with calibration-null false-alarm share <= 0.10, the highest calibration hit rate, ties to the smaller index; else the strictest value, flagged INFEASIBLE. QLIKE: regime-conditional forecast of next-60-min variance, decision bars at or before 15:00 (12:00 on early closes); Diebold-Mariano test. Historical anchors (Flash Crash 2010-05-06 14:42, 2018-02-05) are descriptive; COVID only in evaluation. Hindsight segmentation is secondary.

5.7 No screening beyond Section 4; the pilot drops only zero-variance features. Open item N.3 (selection on all of TRAIN) is a disclosure with the justification of A8 item 4; no in-fold recomputation.

5.8 Per fold, own validation only; the test segment never informs selection. Greedy forward from the return-only model, fixed K=3 / lambda=39, 1 start; stop when the relative QLIKE gain is under 1% or at 6 features; then tune K/lambda with 3 starts. Objective: validation QLIKE; tie-breaks: fewer features, then synthetic delay, then dictionary order. In the implementation the synthetic delay is not computed during the search (A10 item 1), so it does not break ties. Budget exhausted: keep the best so far, record it. All folds if the budget allows, else every 2nd (by amendment). Final setup for 5.13: feature count = median across folds rounded half up (A9 item 3), filled by selection frequency, ties by dictionary order; K/lambda = mode, ties to the smaller value.

5.9 H1 scored per fold on that fold's own selected setup, on its test segment: (a) pAUC(features) - pAUC(baseline), (b) mean QLIKE(baseline) - mean QLIKE(features) with the Diebold-Mariano statistic per fold; paired block bootstrap over consecutive folds (block 3; centred, one-sided, add-one correction) is the primary p-value of each component (A9 item 3), plus Wilcoxon, plus sign consistency, reported beside it. Per family the intersection-union p-value is the larger of the two component p-values. Cross-family comparison is descriptive.

5.10 Robustness: by era; LEGACY +5/+10 min delay; 3 seeds; 1/15-min grids; RAW sensitivity set; threshold +/-0.05.

5.11 Holm: H1 across the three H1 families (BOCPD excluded); H2 across 4 assets. BH for secondary. Power: simulated minimum detectable effects.

5.12 Freeze final setups, thresholds and hashes before any evaluation output exists (hashed freeze document, never overwritten, refused once evaluation output exists). The H2 primary detector = the family passing H1 with the lowest median VALIDATION QLIKE; ties go to the simpler model, order Gaussian HMM < Student-t HMM < HSMM (A9 item 2); BOCPD cannot be the H2 primary detector.

5.13 Refit the frozen setup on full TRAIN per era; run once on the exposed evaluation periods; no retuning (guarded runner: freeze hash verified, token equal to the freeze hash, one run per era). Fold tests are development evidence; 5.13 is confirmatory.

## Added sections (from the amendments)

5.14 Contamination and the confirmatory fold set (A8 item 2, A8.2). A session is touched if an analysis fitted a model on it, scored a detector on it (or on a splice built from it), inspected detector output on it, or used it for a statistic that informed a protocol decision; embargo sessions included. The list is generated mechanically by `section5/s5_contamination.py` from a registry of every script that loads data (a unit test fails if one is missing); D6, which ran no detector, is descriptive and not counted (A8.2). A fold whose post-embargo test segment intersects the list is excluded from confirmatory H1; an all-folds sensitivity is reported. Result at freeze: 6 of 34 folds excluded (LEGACY 27, 28, 29; RAW 1, 2, 3); 28 folds confirmatory; 112 eligible FOMC events for H1(c) (`section5/results/contamination_list.json`). A7 stays in force, disclosed as decided after the RAW fold 3 test curves of the A6 pilot had been scored.

5.15 Construction gate record (A8 item 1, A8.1-A8.4). The R = 1 placebo is the zero-effect reference (A8.1); the gate checks that two independent placebo sets agree (day-level bootstrap of stable days, A8.2). Seed-777 result: RAW 3 passed 8 of 8, LEGACY 29 failed (5 of 8). Characterization over 20 further seeds (A8.3): detectors above 2x RAW's failure rate: Gaussian HMM base and HSMM f3 (3/20 against 1/20 and 0/20). Investigation (A8.4): P(at least 2 of 8 exceed by chance) = 0.152 under the permutation test, above the pre-stated 10%; no single driving day. Per the pre-stated rule the result is documented and the run proceeds. The gate failure on LEGACY 29 is not resolved as a finding; it is carried as a documented limitation.

5.16 Implementation and machinery (A9, A10). Orchestration `section5/s5_run.py` with code-version-keyed checkpoints; selection `s5_select.py`; statistics `s5_stats.py`; H1 scoring `s5_h1.py`; freeze and guarded runner `s5_freeze.py`; H1(c) scoring functions `s5_h1c.py`; data backend `s5_backend.py`. Machinery checks may use only the contaminated folds (RAW 3, LEGACY 29); the backend refuses any other fold and any session outside a fold's own segments. The machinery check passed on both (`A10_MACHINERY_REPORT.md`).

## Open items at freeze (not decided; need an amendment before the step that depends on them)

- The era-level numeric threshold for 5.13 is not defined: A7 fixes the rule on validation sessions of a fold, not on a single full-TRAIN refit.
- Cold audit findings not resolved by A6-A10 remain open as listed in `section5_cold_audit.md` (including 6 EM tolerance, 7 old state re-based during the refractory period, 9 tau cap of the break splices, 10 Lee-Mykland threshold, 11 for the pilot scripts' checkpoint keys, 12-22).
- The A10 backend tunes K in {2, 3, 4} for the HSMM, but 5.4 gives HSMM K 2-3 (the Gaussian and Student-t HMM range 2-4 is consistent). This deviation of the A10 code from 5.4 is unresolved; the 5.4 text stands, and an amendment or a code fix is needed before any run that tunes the HSMM.
- H1(c) hit window assumes the 14:00 release minute (some earlier releases were at 14:15).
"""
P.write_text(T, encoding="utf-8"); P.with_suffix(".sha256").write_text(f"{sha(P)}  {P.name}\n", encoding="ascii"); V0.with_suffix(".sha256").write_text(f"{sha(V0)}  {V0.name}\n", encoding="ascii"); print("frozen", sha(P))
